    "created_at": "2018-09-19T13:55:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-09-19T13:55:28Z",
    "body": "If there was ever a peer-review process and any names were ever ratified, could the status of those names be changed on the wiki page to \"Ratified\"?\r\n\r\nIf there was never a peer-review process and there are no imminent plans to have one, then could the list of status terms in the Standard page be changed to define the three terms that are actually used on the wiki page?\r\n\r\nAlso, it appears that all of the entries in each of the three tables has the same status, but I can't be sure of that because there are so many entries in the first table. If it is true that each table has all the same status, could the status column be removed from each table and replaced with a note preceding each table stating that \"the following table lists all names with status X\"?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
